WEBVTT

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:08.100
I need to concentrate. My chance will come soon.

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:09.310
Sera!

00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:13.010
There it is! A nice pass.

00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:15.520
This is my chance!

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:17.520
I'll make it count!

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:20.530
Here goes!

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:36.460
Sera...

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:40.830
Sakai!

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:50.090
Take up the same position and maintain the pressure.

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:33.010
Oh, really?

00:03:33.410 --> 00:03:36.790
Sera only has a slight sprain? That's a relief.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:43.470
Yeah, but he'll have to rest for a week.

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:46.270
He's young though, so he'll recover quickly.

00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:50.450
A week, huh?

00:03:50.990 --> 00:03:54.410
Our match against Shimizu yesterday ended all square.

00:03:54.410 --> 00:03:58.480
We needed to keep the momentum going, but ended up losing a forward instead.

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:00.230
It's going to be hard.

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:02.160
Right, Coach?

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:03.760
Yeah.

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:09.260
Oh man, I didn't get any of our players.

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:11.350
What are you doing?

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:13.420
Are there manager cards in these, too?

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:16.840
How would I know?! And we're discussing something serious right now!

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:19.270
Why are you always like this?!

00:04:19.270 --> 00:04:20.930
Relax, it's alright.

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:24.050
What's important is that Sera's injury isn't serious.

00:04:24.670 --> 00:04:27.170
The season's just started.

00:04:27.170 --> 00:04:29.940
We mustn't panic just because of this.

00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:37.010
So how's Sera doing?

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:41.200
He's usually very loud,

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:47.450
but he seems to be dejected right now.

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:04.830
I'm such an idiot. What am I doing?

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:07.960
I should be doing my best to hold on to my first-team status,

00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:10.240
but I screwed myself up instead.

00:05:26.950 --> 00:05:29.880
Oh man, this is too much.

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:36.260
Even God is telling me that ETU's main forward should be Natsu.

00:05:37.630 --> 00:05:40.470
If I were really a top player,

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:45.640
I wouldn't have injured myself right when my chance came.

00:05:53.590 --> 00:05:58.990
I guess that's all I've got.

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:08.780
You'll be putting on weight if you keep eating greasy stuff.

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:11.170
S-Sakai...

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:15.230
But whatever, that's just what I need.

00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:19.300
With you out of the picture, I'll finally get a chance to be in the starting line-up.

00:06:19.590 --> 00:06:23.140
Eat more and get fatter. Be injured longer.

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:27.140
He doesn't mince his words, as usual.

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:30.640
Oh, are you about to head home, Sakai?

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:36.700
What, is there a problem with that?

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:41.100
Uh no, it's just that everybody's gone when I finished my medical examination.

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:43.960
Wait, why are you so angry?

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:49.160
I was getting a preventative massage.

00:06:49.940 --> 00:06:54.490
It can't be helped. I'm already 31.

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:57.670
It's tough enough for me just to maintain my physical condition.

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:03.040
And here you are eating potato chips!

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:07.560
Kuroda and Sugie were also talking about eating ramen! Stop screwing around!

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:10.850
Geez... Just because you're young,

00:07:10.850 --> 00:07:12.940
you get carried away and ignore your diet.

00:07:13.270 --> 00:07:15.440
That's why you get injured when it matters.

00:07:19.550 --> 00:07:21.570
I can't even rebuke the argument.

00:07:22.760 --> 00:07:24.530
Just remain the way you are.

00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:28.080
If I play, I'll score your share of the goals too.

00:07:29.650 --> 00:07:31.450
Damn!

00:07:34.330 --> 00:07:35.580
But still,

00:07:37.420 --> 00:07:39.950
I would have taken that shot, too.

00:07:42.010 --> 00:07:45.340
I'll bet Matsu yelled at you.

00:07:47.080 --> 00:07:51.240
That time, Tsubaki was unmarked behind you.

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:56.150
Instead, you forced a shot and hurt yourself.

00:07:57.710 --> 00:08:00.420
But you know you had to.

00:08:00.760 --> 00:08:02.960
You didn't consider the possibility of getting hurt.

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:06.620
We're forwards after all.

00:08:09.790 --> 00:08:13.730
Forwards are like that.

00:08:14.440 --> 00:08:16.930
We put goal-scoring above everything else.

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:23.230
Don't get me wrong me, Sera.

00:08:23.900 --> 00:08:26.500
I'm only sympathizing you,

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:29.550
since I can understand the feelings of a fellow forward.

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:33.390
I might be past my prime.

00:08:34.210 --> 00:08:39.470
I'm neither as strong as Natsuki nor as fast as you,

00:08:40.180 --> 00:08:44.150
but I don't think I'm inferior compared to the both of you.

00:08:44.930 --> 00:08:47.170
I have no intention of giving up.

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:51.910
So how about you, Sera?

00:08:53.910 --> 00:08:56.170
Have you've already admitted defeat to Natsuki?

00:08:59.570 --> 00:09:02.800
If that's the case, it's over for you.

00:09:06.950 --> 00:09:08.760
It's over, the end.

00:09:12.220 --> 00:09:14.060
You know, the ball...

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:22.440
...will always roll towards the person who never gives up.

00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:25.530
That's what I think.

00:09:33.620 --> 00:09:35.450
I won't give up either!

00:09:37.510 --> 00:09:40.210
It's fine, just continue eating your chips.

00:09:40.210 --> 00:09:41.330
I won't!

00:09:41.330 --> 00:09:42.540
Once in a while is fine.

00:09:42.540 --> 00:09:44.240
No, enough is enough!

00:09:44.240 --> 00:09:45.510
Don't hold back.

00:09:45.510 --> 00:09:48.220
I don't want 'em. You can have 'em instead.

00:09:57.970 --> 00:09:59.850
Alright, let's go!

00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:10.450
Unfortunately, I'm not starting, but at least I made the bench.

00:10:10.450 --> 00:10:13.370
I might even get some playing time!

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:36.890
I'm sorry, Hotta.

00:10:37.260 --> 00:10:40.640
Look where you're going, Natsuki.

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:45.650
But still, you're way too excited.

00:10:46.320 --> 00:10:48.720
You're already drenched from doing warm-ups.

00:10:51.150 --> 00:10:54.950
Well, I have to.

00:10:57.470 --> 00:11:01.920
The cheers from the Urawa fans make it look like they're the hosts instead.

00:11:02.780 --> 00:11:05.920
The tension of a goal-less game...

00:11:06.350 --> 00:11:11.100
And on the bench is a lonely samurai who just returned from injury.

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:12.430
Who?

00:11:13.710 --> 00:11:18.180
It's the perfect stage for me to emerge as the hero.

00:11:18.580 --> 00:11:20.900
The perfect stage!

00:11:20.900 --> 00:11:23.190
Don't try to make the manager hear that.

00:11:33.380 --> 00:11:38.330
Damn, Urawa. They started off weakly.

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:41.800
They've adjusted well...

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:46.080
Yeah, their players are linking up well.

00:11:49.390 --> 00:11:52.450
I wonder if we can make them panic again.

00:11:56.220 --> 00:12:00.390
It's a bit early, but I guess now's the time.

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:04.080
Kaneyan, call Natsuki.

00:12:07.380 --> 00:12:11.270
It doesn't feel good when you're not playing.

00:12:11.270 --> 00:12:14.290
I want us to win, but not by a huge margin.

00:12:14.290 --> 00:12:16.490
I don't want us to lose either.

00:12:19.790 --> 00:12:22.730
I shouldn't have gotten myself injured.

00:12:23.240 --> 00:12:24.700
Hey, look!

00:12:32.740 --> 00:12:34.730
He's here!

00:12:35.920 --> 00:12:37.680
We've waited a long time for this!

00:13:02.580 --> 00:13:04.910
Good job, Sakai.

00:13:05.500 --> 00:13:09.330
Just leave everything to me. Everything!

00:13:09.640 --> 00:13:11.680
I'm off then, manager!

00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:14.000
I'll show you my manliness!

00:13:14.460 --> 00:13:17.840
Shut up and go already.

00:13:29.050 --> 00:13:30.530
This is it...

00:13:32.310 --> 00:13:36.260
I've waited eight months for this moment.

00:13:47.890 --> 00:13:52.880
Oh yeah! Come on, Urawa! I'll take you on!

00:13:53.250 --> 00:13:55.690
Bring it!

00:13:57.490 --> 00:14:00.390
I-Is he crying?

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:04.130
Why can't he be more normal?

00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:12.980
Thank you, fans...

00:14:15.570 --> 00:14:18.020
for waiting for me after I took a shot in a strange posture

00:14:18.020 --> 00:14:22.530
and landed awkwardly, resulting in an eight month layoff.

00:14:28.150 --> 00:14:32.780
Thank you, Mr. Goto, for not giving up on me.

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:42.180
Thank you, Doc, my wife and my daughter, for supporting me.

00:14:43.620 --> 00:14:48.680
Thank you, manager, for giving me a chance.

00:14:49.830 --> 00:14:50.950
I'll...

00:14:52.900 --> 00:14:57.480
show them what I can do on the pitch!

00:14:59.940 --> 00:15:01.200
Counter!

00:15:01.600 --> 00:15:02.700
Huh?

00:15:10.030 --> 00:15:11.040
Dori!

00:15:24.260 --> 00:15:25.140
Damn!

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:30.640
Damn, they caught us unaware.

00:15:35.130 --> 00:15:38.650
Huh? The moment I got in?

00:15:40.350 --> 00:15:41.800
That's right.

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:46.070
It's usually like this.

00:15:46.700 --> 00:15:50.960
This is the stage for a real showdown, where you can't let your guard down.

00:15:55.970 --> 00:16:00.740
This is the world I've been dreaming of for the past eight months.

00:16:01.510 --> 00:16:04.630
They will pile on the pressure now that they've got a goal.

00:16:04.630 --> 00:16:07.500
If we don't push forward, we can't score!

00:16:07.500 --> 00:16:13.060
That goal came from your side, Akasaki! Watch out for their counters!

00:16:13.600 --> 00:16:15.640
Stop arguing!

00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:18.310
Push the defense line up a lil' more.

00:16:19.950 --> 00:16:23.730
Hmm... It'll be bad if we continue on like this...

00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:29.830
Nice cover, Tsubaki.

00:16:30.170 --> 00:16:32.050
Damn!

00:16:32.050 --> 00:16:35.830
We'll be playing into their momentum at this rate.

00:16:40.290 --> 00:16:43.550
They're closing down so fast that it's hard to carry the ball forward.

00:16:44.490 --> 00:16:45.930
Hey, I'm free!

00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:51.810
Alright, Natsu, let's set it up from the side.

00:17:25.390 --> 00:17:28.040
Natsuki!

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:32.220
He scored!

00:17:32.860 --> 00:17:35.720
How was that?!

00:17:41.320 --> 00:17:47.730
Natsuki Yotaro! The miraculous comeback kid!

00:17:51.910 --> 00:17:53.240
Yes!

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:56.780
That was an amazing shot by Natsuki!

00:17:56.780 --> 00:18:00.750
He's always so refined when he shoots!

00:18:00.750 --> 00:18:06.460
Natsu's goals always look like a fluke.

00:18:08.460 --> 00:18:14.620
Well, either way, that's how he is.

00:18:16.230 --> 00:18:21.820
It really feels like he's back. Our No.11...

00:18:28.420 --> 00:18:31.520
I did it. I scored!

00:18:37.070 --> 00:18:38.700
This is amazing.

00:18:39.390 --> 00:18:42.230
My little girl fell asleep, but it's still amazing!

00:18:46.760 --> 00:18:50.300
My season starts right now!

00:18:51.300 --> 00:18:56.470
I'll pile up the goals and make up for last year!

00:18:57.660 --> 00:18:59.930
Alright! Let's do this, guys!

00:18:59.930 --> 00:19:04.150
Since when did you take the lead, Natsuki? Quit getting ahead of yourself.

00:19:08.390 --> 00:19:10.540
I'm heading back to put some ice on.

00:19:11.090 --> 00:19:13.350
Otherwise, I might catch a cold.

00:19:13.350 --> 00:19:15.070
Uh, sure.

00:19:19.230 --> 00:19:21.750
Damn, I mustn't lose to him!

00:19:25.330 --> 00:19:28.530
So what? So what?

00:19:30.180 --> 00:19:33.590
He scored right after getting on?!

00:19:37.070 --> 00:19:39.250
You know, the ball...

00:19:40.660 --> 00:19:45.530
will always roll towards the person who never gives up.

00:19:48.400 --> 00:19:49.680
That's right.

00:19:52.240 --> 00:19:55.050
It's only for now, Natsu.

00:19:58.550 --> 00:20:01.890
I'm just letting you catch up a lil'.

00:20:03.220 --> 00:20:06.970
The real battle starts when I'm back in training!

00:20:09.650 --> 00:20:14.010
Heal already, you jerk! I mean, me!

00:20:14.570 --> 00:20:17.670
Natsuki changed the game there.

00:20:18.340 --> 00:20:21.250
He scored when it mattered the most.

00:20:22.510 --> 00:20:27.020
At this point in time, the No.1 forward is unquestionably Natsuki.

00:20:28.040 --> 00:20:30.480
Sakai, Sera, and Natsuki.

00:20:31.180 --> 00:20:35.490
It looks like the battle for the forward position is firing up now.

00:20:36.580 --> 00:20:40.530
Ever since the Nagoya game, ETU have been in good form.

00:20:41.650 --> 00:20:45.750
Plus, Natsuki's comeback will foreshadow even greater things.

00:20:48.190 --> 00:20:51.560
Will this be a fair assumption, Coach?

00:21:01.300 --> 00:21:02.770
A draw?

00:21:02.770 --> 00:21:04.680
Dammit!

00:21:15.460 --> 00:21:18.830
Argh, they were so close!

00:21:18.830 --> 00:21:21.940
That makes it 5 games without loss.

00:21:21.940 --> 00:21:26.490
ETU's pretty good. Right, Yoshi, Shinkichi?

00:21:26.490 --> 00:21:27.830
There are more now...

00:21:38.490 --> 00:21:44.960
We weren't defeated by Urawa, who we've lost to for three straight years.

00:21:44.960 --> 00:21:49.350
Maybe... we've really gotten better.

00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:50.640
Yo.

00:21:50.640 --> 00:21:53.210
That was a great comeback game.

00:21:54.490 --> 00:21:57.580
You think so? You're making me blush.

00:21:57.580 --> 00:21:59.750
Hey, don't get cocky!

00:21:59.750 --> 00:22:01.610
Hey, you two!

00:22:01.610 --> 00:22:04.430
It's not like we've won.

00:22:04.430 --> 00:22:06.120
What's there to fool around?

00:22:06.120 --> 00:22:07.200
Understood!

00:22:07.200 --> 00:22:08.700
Sorry!

00:22:10.530 --> 00:22:15.830
That said though, this may indeed prove that the team's improving.

00:22:17.130 --> 00:22:19.270
Nice goal, Natsuki!

00:22:19.270 --> 00:22:22.140
You did well, let's win the next one!

00:22:26.740 --> 00:22:28.640
What's wrong, Tatsumi?

00:22:29.100 --> 00:22:34.150
The team is doing well, so you should be happy too.

00:22:34.770 --> 00:22:36.510
Well, let's go.

00:22:47.510 --> 00:22:50.160
Doing well, huh?

00:24:15.250 --> 00:24:19.380
I'm not saying that a draw is bad, but...

00:24:20.010 --> 00:24:23.570
Starting tomorrow, we'll be having an intense training programme for the Osaka match.

00:24:24.050 --> 00:24:26.240
What? That's all?
